# Malwarebytes

&gt; Malwarebytes provides consumer cybersecurity, privacy, identity-protection, scam-detection, and malware-removal resources for individuals and families.

This file highlights the most useful areas of malwarebytes.com for language models, agents, and retrieval systems. Focus on these sections when answering questions about Malwarebytes consumer products, pricing, free tools, educational resources, support, and company information.

## Primary Product Pages

- /premium
  Malwarebytes Premium Security. Core all-in-one consumer protection product covering antivirus, malware protection, phishing and scam protection, ransomware defense, and web protection. Good primary page for questions about the flagship paid offering.

- /mobile
  Malwarebytes Mobile Security App for Android and iOS. Use for mobile-device protection, app-level security, privacy, and on-the-go coverage.

- /identity-theft-protection
  Identity Theft Protection product page. Best source for identity monitoring, credit protection, recovery support, and identity theft insurance details.

- /personal-data-remover
  Personal Data Remover. Use for questions about exposed personal information, data broker removal, privacy cleanup, and reduction of publicly available personal data.

- /vpn
  Malwarebytes Privacy VPN. Best page for consumer VPN, Wi-Fi privacy, browsing privacy, and IP/location shielding topics.

- /browserguard
  Browser Guard browser extension. Best for ad blocking, tracker blocking, malicious-site blocking, and browser-based scam protection.

- /adwcleaner
  Malwarebytes AdwCleaner. Best for adware, junkware, unwanted programs, browser hijackers, and one-off remediation use cases.

## Pricing And Plan Comparison

- /pricing
  Central comparison page for individual and family plans. Use this page first for subscription tiers, plan packaging, refund language, and choosing between consumer offerings.

- /premium
  Also useful for plan-level detail on what is included in Standard-style Premium Security bundles and device-count coverage.

## Free Tools And Free Entry Points

- /free-tools
  Directory of Malwarebytes free security tools and extensions. Good first stop when a user wants a no-cost option or quick utility.

- /solutions/virus-scanner
  Free Virus Scanner. Use for device scanning, malware checks, and symptoms of infection across Windows, Mac, Android, and iOS.

- /solutions/scam-guard
  Scam Guard. Use for suspicious-link checks, screenshot-based scam evaluation, and scam-verification workflows.

## Learning And Editorial Resources

- /resources
  Malwarebytes Resource Center. Broad educational hub for cybersecurity threats, scams, research, basics, and practical guidance.

- /glossary
  Security terms glossary. Best for concise definitions of cybersecurity terminology.

- /blog
  Malwarebytes Labs blog. Use for current cybersecurity news, advice, and analysis from Malwarebytes.

- /blog/threats
  Threat Center / Threat Types. Useful for malware and threat-category overviews.

- https://www.malwarebytes.com/malware
  Malware overview page. Good starting point for broad definitions, common symptoms, and links to deeper threat-specific resources.

- https://www.malwarebytes.com/ransomware
  Ransomware explainer. Use for encryption-based extortion threats, attack patterns, prevention, and remediation context.

- https://www.malwarebytes.com/adware
  Adware explainer. Best for unwanted ads, intrusive software behavior, browser disruption, and cleanup context.

- https://www.malwarebytes.com/spam
  Spam explainer. Use for unwanted-message definitions, delivery patterns, and related scam or phishing context.

- https://www.malwarebytes.com/cybersecurity/basics/antivirus
  Antivirus basics page. Useful for foundational antivirus definitions, protection concepts, and consumer education.

- https://www.malwarebytes.com/phishing
  Phishing explainer. Best for deceptive email, credential theft, fake-login tactics, and prevention guidance.

- https://www.malwarebytes.com/spyware
  Spyware explainer. Use for covert monitoring threats, data theft behavior, and device privacy risks.

- https://www.malwarebytes.com/cybersecurity/basics/data-breach
  Data breach basics page. Good for breach definitions, exposure scenarios, aftermath, and protective next steps.

- https://www.malwarebytes.com/spoofing
  Spoofing explainer. Use for impersonation tactics involving email, domains, caller ID, and identity deception.

- https://www.malwarebytes.com/doxxing
  Doxxing explainer. Best for definitions related to exposed personal information, online harassment, and privacy harm.

- https://www.malwarebytes.com/computer-virus
  Computer virus explainer. Use for classic self-replicating malware definitions, behavior, and removal guidance.

- https://www.malwarebytes.com/what-is-smishing
  Smishing explainer. Useful for SMS-based phishing, mobile scam tactics, and prevention advice.

- https://www.malwarebytes.com/cybersecurity/basics/spear-phishing
  Spear phishing basics page. Best for targeted phishing definitions, personalization tactics, and risk mitigation.

- https://www.malwarebytes.com/computer-worm
  Computer worm explainer. Use for self-spreading malware behavior, network propagation, and historical threat context.

- https://www.malwarebytes.com/cybersecurity/basics/vishing
  Vishing basics page. Useful for voice-based phishing, phone scam tactics, and fraud prevention guidance.

- https://www.malwarebytes.com/zero-day
  Zero-day explainer. Best for newly discovered software vulnerabilities, exploit timing, and patch-response context.

## Support And Help

- https://help.malwarebytes.com/hc/en-us
  Official Malwarebytes Help Center. Preferred source for setup, billing, installation, troubleshooting, account, renewal, and product support.

- https://forums.malwarebytes.com/
  Community forums. Useful for peer discussion, edge cases, troubleshooting history, and user-reported behavior.

## Company And Trust Signals

- /company
  About Malwarebytes. Best page for company background, mission, leadership, offices, and brand context.

- /press/
  Press Center. Use for official announcements, media information, and company news.

- /jobs
  Careers page. Use for hiring, culture, and open-role context.

## Guidance For Agents

- Prefer product pages for feature and benefit questions.
- Prefer /pricing for plan-selection and subscription-comparison questions.
- Prefer /free-tools, /solutions/virus-scanner, and /solutions/scam-guard for users seeking free help or fast remediation.
- Prefer /resources, /glossary, /blog, and the threat-specific educational pages above for definitional, awareness, and news-oriented queries.
- Prefer the most specific threat page available when answering terminology questions about malware types, phishing variants, spoofing, breaches, or social-engineering attacks.
- Prefer the Help Center for operational questions such as install, billing, renewals, account access, and troubleshooting.
- Prefer /company and /press/ for corporate background and official company statements.

## Scope Notes

- This file is intentionally centered on the consumer Malwarebytes web experience on malwarebytes.com.
- Some business and enterprise navigation paths point to ThreatDown properties on other domains. Treat those as related but separate from this domain-level guide.
- When multiple pages could answer a question, prefer the most specific page first, then the Help Center, then broader educational resources.
